<title>USA: Coopers &amp; Lybrand names Marsha Cohen CFO.</title>
<headline>Coopers &amp; Lybrand names Marsha Cohen CFO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coopers &amp; Lybrand LLP on Thursday said Marsha Cohen has been named vice chairman and chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Cohen succeeds Frank Scalia as chief financial officer, the company said.  Scalia, who held the post since 1985, is taking over supervision of special international and systems projects.</p>
<p>Cohen's appointment is effective July 1, the company said. Cohen joined the firm in 1976 and has been a partner since 1984.</p>
</text>
